5. How does LangGraph know what to pass?

Every agent has the same function signature:

def reader_agent(state):

    ...

    return state

Example:

Reader Agent

email = state["email"]

summary = llm(...)

state["summary"] = summary

return state

Classification Agent

email = state["email"]

category = llm(...)

state["category"] = category

return state

Policy Agent

knowledge = state["knowledge"]

policy = llm(...)

state["policy_result"] = policy

return state

Each agent:

reads the fields it needs from state
writes new fields back into state
returns the updated state

LangGraph automatically passes this updated state to the next agent in the workflow.

